---
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro'
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro'
import TextPage from '../layouts/TextPage.astro'

/**
 * The help page, which is about one thing: getting past the first launch
 * warning. It is deliberately short.
 *
 * Earlier drafts also carried sections on Intel Macs, updating, uninstalling,
 * soft wallpapers, missing displays and the "is damaged" dialog. Not one of
 * those had ever been reported by a user; they came from search queries. They
 * were cut. Anything added back should answer a question somebody asked.
 *
 * The dialog strings are quoted verbatim, ".app" included, because people paste
 * them into a search box. Do not tidy them.
 */
const sections = [
  { id: 'requirements', title: 'System requirements' },
  { id: 'first-launch', title: 'Apple could not verify SpreadPaper.app is free of malware' },
  { id: 'still-stuck', title: 'Questions, problems and ideas' },
]

const warningAlt =
  'The macOS warning dialog, titled "SpreadPaper.app" Not Opened, reading: Apple could not verify "SpreadPaper.app" is free of malware that may harm your Mac or compromise your privacy. Move to Trash is the highlighted default button, with Done below it.'

const dmgAlt =
  'The SpreadPaper disk image open in Finder, with the SpreadPaper app icon beside a shortcut to the Applications folder, which is what you drag it onto.'

const breadcrumb = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Help', path: '/help' },
]
---

<TextPage
  title="SpreadPaper Help: Install, Open and Fix Problems on macOS"
  description="How to get past the macOS warning the first time you open SpreadPaper, through System Settings or with one Terminal command, and where to ask if you are stuck."
  socialDescription="Getting past the macOS warning the first time you open SpreadPaper."
  eyebrow="Help"
  heading="Installing SpreadPaper on macOS and fixing common problems"
  lead="SpreadPaper is not signed with a paid Apple Developer ID, so macOS blocks the first launch. Allow it once and you are done."
  breadcrumb={breadcrumb}
>
  <Prose>
    <nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="on-this-page">
      <p id="on-this-page"><strong>On this page</strong></p>
      <ul>
        {sections.map((section) => <li><a href={`#${section.id}`}>{section.title}</a></li>)}
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="requirements">System requirements</h2>
    <dl class="dl split">
      <div>
        <dt>macOS</dt>
        <dd>15.0 Sequoia or later</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Mac</dt>
        <dd>Apple silicon</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Displays</dt>
        <dd>Any number, any arrangement</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Account</dt>
        <dd>None</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <h2 id="first-launch">Apple could not verify SpreadPaper.app is free of malware</h2>
    <p>Nothing was scanned and nothing was found. macOS looked for a paid developer signature, did not find one, and stopped. Every release is built from public source by GitHub Actions.</p>
    <p>First, drag SpreadPaper into Applications. Both routes below need it there.</p>

    <figure class="wide">
      <img src="/help/dmg-drag-to-applications.png" width="1220" height="430" alt={dmgAlt} />
      <figcaption>Drag the app onto the Applications shortcut beside it.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p>Open it from Applications and macOS shows this:</p>

    <figure>
      <img src="/help/gatekeeper-warning.png" width="520" height="384" alt={warningAlt} />
      <figcaption>"SpreadPaper.app" Not Opened. Apple could not verify "SpreadPaper.app" is free of malware that may harm your Mac or compromise your privacy.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="note note-accent">
      <p><strong>Click Done, not Move to Trash.</strong> Move to Trash is the blue default, so it is the one your eye lands on. It deletes the app.</p>
    </div>

    <p>Then take either route. Once, and only the first time.</p>

    <div class="routes">
      <section class="route">
        <h3>Open it from System Settings, Privacy and Security</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Open SpreadPaper from Applications, then click <strong>Done</strong>.</li>
          <li>Go to System Settings, Privacy and Security, and scroll to <strong>Security</strong>.</li>
          <li>Click <strong>Open Anyway</strong>.</li>
          <li>Enter your login password, the one you sign in to your Mac with.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Done. It opens normally from now on.</p>

        <div class="note note-accent">
          <p>Right click and Open no longer works. Apple removed it in Sequoia, so older guides are wrong.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="route">
        <h3>Or remove the quarantine flag in Terminal</h3>
        <p>Clears the download flag, so no warning appears at all.</p>
        <div class="command flex flex-col gap-3 p-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
          <code id="quarantine-command" class="cd-code min-w-0 flex-1 break-words py-1 pl-1">xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/SpreadPaper.app</code>
          <button type="button" hidden data-copy-target="quarantine-command" data-copy-label="Copy" data-copied-label="Copied" class="cd-button cd-button-secondary h-11 shrink-0 gap-1.5 px-3 text-xs focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-cd-accent focus-visible:outline-offset-2"><Icon name="copy" data-copy-icon="idle" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" /><Icon name="check" data-copy-icon="done" hidden class="h-3.5 w-3.5" /><span data-copy-text aria-live="polite">Copy</span><span class="sr-only"> the quarantine command</span></button>
        </div>
        <p>The path must be exactly that. Renamed, or still in Downloads, and it silently does nothing.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <h3>No Open Anyway button?</h3>
    <p>It only appears after you try to open the app, and only for about an hour. Open SpreadPaper again, click Done, then go straight back to Privacy and Security. Per <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-om/guide/mac-help/mh40617/mac">Apple</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="still-stuck">Questions, problems and ideas</h2>
    <div class="closing">
      <div>
        <p>Bezel compensation, presets, schedules: each one started as somebody opening an issue. Questions, bugs and ideas all go to the same place.</p>
        <div class="actions flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <a href="https://github.com/spreadpaper/SpreadPaper/issues" class="cd-button cd-button-primary h-11 px-6 text-[0.9375rem] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-cd-accent focus-visible:outline-offset-2">
            <Icon name="github-logo" width="18" height="18" />
            Open an issue on GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p>Reporting a bug? Include your macOS version, from System Settings, General, About, and your SpreadPaper version, from the app's About window.</p>
        <p>No GitHub account? <a href="mailto:hello@spreadpaper.app">hello@spreadpaper.app</a> reaches the same person.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Prose>
</TextPage>
